  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\nWell above normal temperatures are expected for Thursday with highs\nareawide in the 80s. A few 90 degree readings cannot be ruled out\nnear and south of the Ohio River. Temperatures will fall on Friday as\na cold front moves through, ushering in generally below normal\ntemperatures for the remainder of the week. There will be the\npotential for some patchy frost Monday night into Tuesday morning.\n\nKey Message 2)\nA few light showers or sprinkles cannot be ruled out this afternoon\nthrough the overnight across far northern portions of the region\nnorth of Interstate 70. Most of this will be falling from a mid deck\nhowever and therefore do not expect much if any to reach the ground.\nDue to that left NBM dry forecast in place.\n\nShowers will move into the region Thursday evening through Friday\nbefore tapering off Friday evening. This is associated with a cold\nfront that will move through the area. There is some limited\ninstability and therefore have a lower end thunder mention in part of\nthe forecast area as well. While brief periods of heavy rain will be\npossible, the probability of flooding conditions is low at this time\nand therefore left any mention out of the HWO.",
